void SetCellAlignment(int row, int col, Alignment h, Alignment v);  Row/column counts come from SetColumnCount/SetRowCount (or SetColumnStretch/SetRowStretch ); empty tracks still exist , so no placeholder children are needed. SetCellAlignment controls how a child sits inside its own cell (default Stretch ); SetHorizontalAlignment/SetVerticalAlignment align the whole grid content in the leftover space. A 1×1 grid can also use content alignment; SetColumnStretch(2, ...) creates a third column. Without explicit row/col stretch, the cell weight is the max of spanned children's weights. Version : since v1.26.0 , an explicit SetWidth/SetHeight on the Grid is also used as the cell measurement scope; it no longer reports 260 while arranging rows at 274+.

