void RemoveKeyHandler(int id);  Called after OnWindowKeyDown and before the focused element; returning true marks the key handled. Handlers run in registration order; AddKeyHandler returns an id and RemoveKeyHandler(id) unregisters it. For temporary Esc handling in drawers/popups; remove on close/detach/destruction. Version : v1.25.0 .  Pitfall every key press copies a handler snapshot first; calling RemoveKeyHandler inside a callback does not cancel the current pass, and a just-removed handler may still run once. returning true swallows the key: the focused element and later handlers never see it. Do not unconditionally consume Tab/Enter/Esc. handlers usually capture a raw this ; the owner must remove them before destruction, otherwise a live window can call back into a dangling object ( Drawer handles this automatically). handlers run on the UI thread; do not block for long and do not add/remove them from other threads.

