void Open/Close/Toggle();  bool IsOpen/IsAnimating() const;  float GetOpenProgress() const;  Overlay Rounded scrim over content; dismiss with outside click or Esc. Good for navigation and filters. Push Content yields while the panel is open and participates in layout; good for list + detail side by side. Permanent Always open, no animation/scrim, Close ignored; good for persistent navigation or settings.  Recommended Use Drawer as the root layout or a GridLayout cell; Overlay for temporary content, Push when content should shrink, Permanent for long-lived navigation. Put panel content in SetPanel and the main content in SetContent .  Paint order SetPanelShadow is painted before the panel background, so the opaque background covers its inner layers and only the outer shadow remains visible; the border is painted last.  Pitfall SetContent is the main content (covered/yielded by the drawer); SetPanel is the drawer panel. Putting panel content in SetContent skips the panel background, padding, rounded corners and shadow. SetPanelSize is the outer panel size; the default 16 px padding is subtracted from the panel content (e.g. outer 200 leaves 168 for content). Increase SetPanelSize or reduce SetPanelPadding when the panel needs more room. Drawer is a layout control and covers only its own arranged rect (the root layout or one GridLayout cell), not the window title bar/menu bar. Put it at the outermost level of the area you want to dim. Open() sets the target state and raises OpenChanged immediately; Opened / Closed fire only after the animation ends. IsOpen() returns the target state, not the current progress; use IsAnimating() / GetOpenProgress() during a transition. Permanent forces open, progress 1, no animation/scrim; Close() / SetOpen(false) are ignored. Switching back to Overlay/Push does not auto-close ; call Close() explicitly. the scrim exists only in Overlay; SetDismissOnScrimClick / ScrimClicked work only with SetModal(true) and progress > 0. With SetModal(false) , clicks reach the content and ScrimClicked never fires. SetScrimOpacity(0) makes the scrim visually transparent but keeps modal hit-testing (clicks are still blocked); use SetModal(false) for click-through. SetContentBorder is drawn only in Overlay; Push/Permanent have no content border. The inner layers of SetPanelShadow are covered by the opaque panel background; only the outer shadow remains, and the border is painted last. Esc handling and SetFocusOnOpen require the Drawer to be attached to a Window ; before attach, no Esc handler is registered and focus is not applied.  Version : v1.25.0 .

