Header ZufyUIHwndView.h (auto-included at the end of ZufyUIWindowTool.h ). Embeds a WebView2 HWND controller, camera/capture window, third-party native control, or an out-of-process window into the ZufyUI layout.  cpp Copy class HwndView : public UIElement { public : explicit HwndView ( HWND owner , bool activate = false ); HWND GetHostHwnd () const ; void SetContentHwnd ( HWND external , bool own = false ); HWND GetContentHwnd () const ; void SetObscured ( bool on ); bool IsObscured () const ; void SetOnBoundsChanged ( std :: function < void ( HWND , int , int ) > ); }; class HwndView : public UIElement {
public:
    explicit HwndView(HWND owner, bool activate = false);
    HWND GetHostHwnd() const;
    void SetContentHwnd(HWND external, bool own = false);
    HWND GetContentHwnd() const;
    void SetObscured(bool on);
    bool IsObscured() const;
    void SetOnBoundsChanged(std::function<void(HWND, int, int)>);
};  Implementation: creates a normal Win32 top-level owned popup as the host; SetContentHwnd re-parents the external HWND as its WS_CHILD (cross-thread/cross-process allowed) and shows it explicitly. Moving/resizing the host moves the child natively; the host client clips it, plus SetWindowRgn (element rect ∩ window client ∩ every ancestor GetClipRect , incl. the ScrollViewer viewport). Cross-process risk : cross-process SetParent is technically legal but not recommended: it couples the input queues (one stuck process can freeze the other), blocks some window messages, can be intermittently unstable, and the target process may not know its window was re-parented. Prefer same-process ; use cross-process only as a last resort. Convention : for "content goes into composition, no airspace" (web/video) use CreateExternalVisual below / WebView2 CompositionController .  Pitfall the main window is WS_EX_NOREDIRECTIONBITMAP + DComp , so child HWNDs are not composited ; do not use a normal child control. HwndView is an airspace overlay — always above the window content; in-window dropdowns/tooltips cannot cover it (menus are separate top-level windows and are unaffected).

For WebView2 CompositionController, video/capture, or anything that renders into DComp .  cpp Copy IUnknown * Window::CreateExternalVisual (); void Window::SetExternalVisualBounds ( IUnknown * visual , float x , float y , float w , float h ); void Window::RemoveExternalVisual ( IUnknown * visual ); int Window::AddOverlaySync ( std :: function < void () > ); void Window::RemoveOverlaySync ( int id ); void Window::SyncOverlays (); IUnknown* Window::CreateExternalVisual();
