void Window::SyncOverlays();  Returns a WinRT ContainerVisual (inserted at the top of the root visual) to pass to controller->put_RootVisualTarget(visual) ; set its position/size in Arrange via SetExternalVisualBounds (DIP, converted to physical pixels internally). AddOverlaySync/RemoveOverlaySync/SyncOverlays let external-window hosts (e.g. HwndView ) register a sync callback; usually not called directly.  Pitfall on device loss/rebuild the visual tree is recreated → listen to Window::DeviceLost , call CreateExternalVisual again and re-attach.

